[gd_scene load_steps=7 format=3 uid="uid://b6unitrig4444"]

; The sprite rig's own scene — ADR-0217 dec. 3, built by #744. The base that
; `res://assets/scenes/Unit.tscn` INHERITS, and the addon's one declared mount in
; `check_lattice_scene.py`.
;
; 🔴 WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `Unit.tscn` named four addon paths by `ext_resource` after the
; move — the shader plus three scripts — and 114 files reference `Unit.tscn` (5
; production, 109 `tests/`). Collapsing the four to one instance line is what lets those
; 109 tests never learn the addon exists. The façade deliberately does NOT also publish
; this scene: `const UnitRig = preload(...)` would resolve fine and give the rig two
; spellings of one publish, so pass 9 would have two numbers for one question (ADR-0205
; dec. 2 forbids exactly that merge).
;
; 🔴 INHERITED, NOT INSTANCED — ADR-0204's form, not ADR-0207 dec. 2's. The host adds five
; nodes of its own to this root (`ShadowMesh`, `ShadowRaycast`, `SelectionArea`,
; `MovementComponent`, `UnitStats`, `EquippedAbilities`, `UnitStatusManager`) and every one
; of `Unit.tscn`'s node paths has to stay byte-identical, because `Unit.gd` and its
; consumers address them by name. A wrapper node would bury all of them one level deeper.
;
; 🔴 THE MATERIAL CARRIES NO TEXTURES, AND THAT IS THE POINT (P4). `Unit.tscn` authored
; `type1_tex`/`wep1_tex`/`eff1_tex` against `res://assets/sprites/textures/{01,WEP1,EFF1}.tga`
; — three host content addresses that would move INTO the addon with the mesh and put P4
; back above zero on the day #744 drove it to zero. They are not a loss: `Unit.gd`
; `_initialize_materials()` REPLACES this material outright —
; `self.material = UnitAssets.base_material().duplicate()` then
; `self.mesh_instance.mesh.surface_set_material(0, material)` — so nothing at runtime has
; ever read a texture authored here. `SpriteLayerManager` then binds the body sheet per
; unit (`load_sprite_texture`) and lazily loads WEP1/EFF1 through
; `SpriteRigContentRoot`. The authored block is an EDITOR PREVIEW, and the preview it
; gives now is an untextured quad rather than Ramza.
;
; The remaining `shader_parameter/` block is kept byte-identical to what `Unit.tscn`
; carried, minus those three lines: it is equally overwritten, and changing it here would
; mix a rendering change into a move.

